Z||000000||bHooper||04-03-2001||07:10 PM||||anyone ever use this stuff?  <P>i've been giving it some consideration today, as the oil pressure was a little low at idle, last night, on the GT.... like 20 PSI!<P>the car has never <B>EVER</B> had low oil pressure b4.  the needle has always been jumpy, and i just have atributed that to a $39 oil pressure sending unit, that i have delayed replacement of.<P>anyway, the price of th e"do it yourself" kit is far better than the $100 from precision tune!<P>thanks!<BR>hoop||||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||04-03-2001||07:44 PM||||Its just repackaged and marked up karosine (sp?). It is a far better deal then $100 for a shop to do it though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-03-2001||08:30 PM||||i usually drain 1 qt of oil and add a can of trans fluid. It really cleans out. Just drive it a few miles, then drain it and put in new filter and oil. Ive had low oil pressure show up when the oil is dirty, clogs up the pinhole in sending unit, replaced the sending unit and pressure showed normal.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||04-03-2001||09:32 PM||||Be VERY careful about flushing the oil system with a solvent or high detergent fluid (like trans fluid) I did that once, and was troubleshooting no oil pressure two weeks later. What I wasn't aware of was that the previous owner had used Quaker State, and there was an enormous amount of parafin buildup in the motor. Ran the cleaner through the motor, and it washed a bunch of that mess into the oil pan, and it got sucked up into the oil pump strainer. No oil pressure. Bad thing. I would STRONGLY suggest that after running the cleaner through, the pan be removed to clean out the debris and shrapnel that will no doubt collect there.<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||04-03-2001||09:35 PM||||so you <I>drive</I> the car with the tranny fluid in the engine?!!!  how far...10 miles, 20? 30?<P>supposedly, your supposed to just let the engine run for 10-15 min. with that in it.<P>the precision tune method is $100 because they do it under presure, hooked up to some contraption.<P>btw, cranked the car and let it run for 1-15 min. tonight, with no oil pressure problems.  but it is understood that that is no where near the equivilant of 30 min. of my driving!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||04-03-2001||09:47 PM||||thought well taken, tai!<P>however, i don't believe that i have ever used a parafin based oil, in 80,000 miles.  i know that i have used, valvoline, havoline, and whatever BP's oil is. (i think)<P>i could probably count on one hand the places that have done the oil changes since i purchased it.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||04-03-2001||09:59 PM||||Hoop:<P>On the blue GT the pressure is very high when cold and normally runs 50 60 psi on the in car gauge at highway speeds.  My problem is at hot idle, it will sit at about 20-25, and occassionally flash the pressure warning light momentarily.  I haven't replaced the sending unit on this car yet, and I plan to replace the bypass valve if I can find it when I do my next oil change.  <P>Will let you know if it helps.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
